BT /F1 13 Tf 72 750 Td 15 TL (2. Diversity estimator selection) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 728 Td 12 TL
(Aggregate counted frames per site. Let n be the count of accepted detections, S the number) Tj T*
(of distinct accepted species, and count_i the count for species i, with p_i = count_i / n.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Report Shannon entropy in nats: H = -sum\(p_i * ln p_i\). Report Simpson diversity as the) Tj T*
(Gini-Simpson probability that two interspecific draws differ, D = 1 - sum\(p_i^2\). These are) Tj T*
(the office standards; the base-2 entropy and inverse-Simpson forms answer different) Tj T*
(questions and are not the reported quantities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For richness, the office standard is the finite-sample bias-corrected Chao estimator ChaoBC) Tj T*
(= S + f1*\(f1-1\)/\(2*\(f2+1\)\), where f1 and f2 count species with one and two detections. It is) Tj T*
(selected because it stays finite when f2 = 0, a singleton-heavy profile present in the) Tj T*
(staged data. The classic S + f1^2/\(2*f2\) has no finite value there and is not used.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Record these choices in /app/output/method_choices.csv with a short justification tied to) Tj T*
(the calibration sheet or the count profile, as specified in the instruction. The record is) Tj T*
(graded alongside the estimates.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
